  "result": "I'd make it easier for people to change their minds without feeling like they've lost something.\n\nSo much human conflict, from family arguments to political deadlock to institutions that refuse to fix known mistakes, persists because admitting error feels like a loss of face, identity, or standing. If updating your views were cheap and even admired, people could settle disagreements faster, correct bad policies sooner, and apologize without it costing them so much. Many problems might become much more solvable.\n\nI'm not sure it's the most important change. Ending preventable disease or poverty would arguably matter more. But I think a world where people hold beliefs more loosely and revise them more readily would be better at finding and fixing its other problems.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
